# Testing & Verification Standards

## Test-Driven Development (TDD)
- Red-Green-Refactor: Write failing automated tests first, implement minimal passing code, then refactor cleanly.
- Mock Avoidance: Prefer real in-memory databases (SQLite) and contract-tested interfaces over brittle mocks.
- Flaky Test Ban: Never swallow exceptions or use empty catch blocks. Implement condition-based waiting for async events.
- Verification Gates: Run automated test suites before claiming any task completion.
- Reference Skills: Consult `./.agent/skills/test-driven-development/SKILL.md` and `./.agent/skills/testing-patterns/SKILL.md`.
